# Backend Resilience Services

Import from `UtilsModule` — do not build parallel locking, transaction, or circuit-breaker logic.

| Service | Method | Use when |
|---------|--------|----------|
| `MutexService` | `execWithMutex(resourceId, fn)` | Only one worker/process should run a critical section (e.g. per-entity exclusive work) |
| `DbTransactionsService` | `exec(fn)` | Multiple MongoDB writes must commit or roll back together |
| `CircuitBreakersService` | `executeWithCircuitBreaker(name, fn)` | External HTTP/API calls that should trip open after repeated failures |

## Rules

- **Mutex** — pass a stable `resourceId` (entity ID, job key). Callback runs exclusively for that key.
- **Transactions** — pass async function receiving a session; keep scope small.
- **Circuit breaker** — use a consistent breaker name per integration; admin can reset via `CircuitBreakersController`.
- Outbound HTTP — extend `BaseApiService` (backend) for Axios logging and rate-limit `ErrorCode` handling.

## Do not build

- Custom lock collections or in-memory mutexes
- Manual MongoDB session plumbing
- Ad-hoc retry/circuit logic per call site

